{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And they were a bitterness of spirit.</b> They were like a razor and knife cutting short the lives of Isaac and Rebekah. The term מורת is like וּמוֹרָה לֹא יַעֲלֶה עַל רֹאשׁוֹ (Judges 13:5). Now despite all this, Isaac did not recognize the extent of Esau's wickedness, in that he did not rebuke him for them. In this he stumbled, for he sought to bless Esau, and from there came the stumbling that he gave Esau some blessing or counsel that greatly increased hatred between his sons, and that necessitated Jacob's flight to another land."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:31:54.845579977Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}